Standards for Imposition of Administrative Fines (Related to Article 21)
■ Enforcement Decree of the Act on Promotion of Periodicals, Including Magazines [Appendix] <Amended on Jun. 8, 2016>

Standards for Imposition of Administrative Fines (Related to Article 21)

1. General standards
(a) The imposing authority may reduce the administrative fine prescribed in item 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases. This shall not apply, however, to an offender who is in arrears with administrative fines.
1) Where the offender falls under any subparagraph of Article 2-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Regulation of Violations of Public Order.
2) Where the violation is recognized as resulting from minor negligence or error.
3) Where a reduction is otherwise deemed necessary in view of the severity, motive and consequences of the violation.
(b) The imposing authority may increase the administrative fine prescribed in item 2 by up to one-half in any of the following cases. The amount shall not, however, exceed the maximum administrative fine under Article 33 of the Act.
1) Where the same violation is detected again within one year from the date on which an administrative fine was imposed.
2) Where the violation has caused serious damage to another magazine publisher or subscribers.
3) Where the violation of statutes or regulations has continued for at least one month.
4) Where an increase is otherwise deemed necessary in view of the severity, motive and consequences of the violation.

2. Individual standards
| Violation | Statutory basis | Administrative fine |
|---|---|---|
| (a) Editing in violation of Article 6 of the Act | Article 33 (1) 1 of the Act | 5,000,000 won |
| (b) Failure to report closure of business in violation of Article 17 of the Act | Article 33 (2) 1 of the Act | 2,500,000 won |
| (c) Failure to state required particulars in violation of Article 19 of the Act | Article 33 (1) 2 of the Act | 4,000,000 won |
| (d) Taking office as a publisher or editor while falling under any subparagraph of Article 20 (1) of the Act | Article 33 (1) 3 of the Act | 7,000,000 won |
| (e) Appointing a person falling under any subparagraph of Article 20 (1) of the Act as a publisher or editor | Article 33 (1) 4 of the Act | 7,000,000 won |
| (f) Failure to submit, within the prescribed period, documents proving that a report has been filed with the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy, in violation of Article 21 of the Act | Article 33 (2) 2 of the Act | 2,000,000 won |
| (g) Failure to report succession to business within the prescribed period, in violation of Article 22 of the Act | Article 33 (2) 3 of the Act | 1,500,000 won |

